.TH EUCLID-CLI-EQS-PURGE-QUEUE 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eqs-purge-queue \- delete all messages from a queue
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eqs purge-queue
.BR \-\-ern | \-e
.I ERN
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes all messages from a queue identified by its Euclid resource
name (ERN). The queue itself is not deleted; see
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-delete-queue (1)
for that. This cannot be undone.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-ern " " \fIERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the queue to purge. Required.
.PP
The queue may be given by
.B name
instead of by ERN, in which case it is resolved in your session's account
and namespace; see
.B NAMES AND ERNS
in
.BR euclid-cli-eqs (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The queue's messages were deleted. No output is printed.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, or no queue
with that ERN exists.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eqs purge-queue \e
    --ern ern:queues:eu-central-1:000000000000:queue:orders
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eqs (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-purge-all-queues (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-delete-queue (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Jens Vogt <jens.vogt@opitz-consulting.com>
